  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The recent build/test  improvements to automate deploying Fedora instances and running the integration tests on them are a significant improvement.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "But whenever you get something, you always want more!",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Suggestions for some improvements:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "single test config failure prevents other tests running - eg if a test in configA fails, configB/C/Q don't run",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "install from single copy of installer jar - currently installer is copied to locations for configA/B/C/Q - things would run a little faster if we could install from a single copy of the installer rather than needing to copy it to four different locations",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "disabled configs still go through a build, eg -DconfigA=false does result in the tests not running for configA, but it seems to go through a build process; again things would be a little faster if this didn't happen",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Overall desire here is to decrease the round-trip time for fixing an issue with a single integration test case.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
